  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\r\n\r\nAfter #10017 , a native darkmode was added to the spec text itself. However, there are a few types of spec objects that don't seem to respect the theming.\r\n\r\nFor example, the block of properties underneath the definition for the `<style>` element seem to be wrapped in a `<dl>` with `class=\"element\"` that hardcodes the background and text colors from the standard theme, per the following screenshot:\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#the-style-element\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/whatwg/html/assets/8388494/e07cf72b-f37a-4d43-88de-817e56539490)\r\n\r\nThough it's entirely possible this is a Gecko/Ubuntu theming bug :D\r\n\r\nUbuntu 22.04\r\nFirefox 121.0.1 (64-bit) (from Ubuntu Snap)\r\n\r\nAlso seems to repro on firefox and chrome on macOS, so likely a page issue vs a browser one :)\r\n\r\ncc @tabatkins @domenic ",
